    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.ai\r\n\r\n### Question\r\n\r\nI managed to create an insert mode keymap to delete the current subword like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\ncustom_textobjects = {\r\n  e = {\r\n    {\r\n      '%u[%l%d]+%f[^%l%d]',\r\n      '%f[%S][%l%d]+%f[^%l%d]',\r\n      '%f[%P][%l%d]+%f[^%l%d]',\r\n      '^[%l%d]+%f[^%l%d]',\r\n    },\r\n    '^().*()$'\r\n  },\r\n},\r\n```\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.keymap.set(\"i\", \"<C-e>\", function() vim.api.nvim_input(\"<Esc>cie\") end, { desc = \"Delete subword\" })\r\n```\r\n\r\nUsing `<C-o>` or setting the `rhs` as a string does not work. To be honest, I don't know what the problem is and I haven't tried to find it.\r\n\r\nIs this a known issue? ~~Maybe it would be a good idea to document this behavior if it isn't already documented.~~",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.ai</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I managed to create an insert mode keymap to delete the current subword like this:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"custom_textobjects = {\n  e = {\n    {\n      '%u[%l%d]+%f[^%l%d]',\n      '%f[%S][%l%d]+%f[^%l%d]',\n      '%f[%P][%l%d]+%f[^%l%d]',\n      '^[%l%d]+%f[^%l%d]',\n    },\n    '^().*()$'\n  },\n},\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">custom_textobjects</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">e</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n    {\n      <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>%u[%l%d]+%f[^%l%d]<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n      <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>%f[%S][%l%d]+%f[^%l%d]<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n      <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>%f[%P][%l%d]+%f[^%l%d]<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n      <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>^[%l%d]+%f[^%l%d]<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>,\n    },\n    <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>^().*()$<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>\n  },\n},</pre></div>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"vim.keymap.set(&quot;i&quot;, &quot;&lt;C-e&gt;&quot;, function() vim.api.nvim_input(&quot;&lt;Esc&gt;cie&quot;) end, { desc = &quot;Delete subword&quot; })\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">keymap</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">set</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>i<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>&lt;C-e&gt;<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>() <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_input</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>&lt;Esc&gt;cie<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>) <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>, { <span class=\"pl-smi\">desc</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>Delete subword<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>})</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Using <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;C-o&gt;</code> or setting the <code class=\"notranslate\">rhs</code> as a string does not work. To be honest, I don't know what the problem is and I haven't tried to find it.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is this a known issue? <del>Maybe it would be a good idea to document this behavior if it isn't already documented.</del></p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.ai\nQuestion\nI managed to create an insert mode keymap to delete the current subword like this:\ncustom_textobjects = {\n  e = {\n    {\n      '%u[%l%d]+%f[^%l%d]',\n      '%f[%S][%l%d]+%f[^%l%d]',\n      '%f[%P][%l%d]+%f[^%l%d]',\n      '^[%l%d]+%f[^%l%d]',\n    },\n    '^().*()$'\n  },\n},\nvim.keymap.set(\"i\", \"<C-e>\", function() vim.api.nvim_input(\"<Esc>cie\") end, { desc = \"Delete subword\" })\nUsing <C-o> or setting the rhs as a string does not work. To be honest, I don't know what the problem is and I haven't tried to find it.\nIs this a known issue? Maybe it would be a good idea to document this behavior if it isn't already documented.",
